# Force LF line endings on checkout. The ROS2 deployment target is WSL2,
# where a Windows-side git default of core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# convert checked-out text files to CRLF and break the runtime:
#   - a CRLF shebang (#!...\r) makes `ros2 launch` fail with an exec
#     format / bad-interpreter error on the symlinked node scripts,
#   - CRLF YAML is tolerated by rclpy but is a live footgun.
# `text=auto` keeps binaries untouched while normalizing text to LF in the
# repo; the per-type eol=lf lines pin the *checkout* byte stream to LF so
# autocrlf cannot re-corrupt them.
* text=auto
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
